      "rev_n_1_dc039c_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_dc039c_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_dc039c",
        "thought_text": "Thought-1: The current greedy approach fails because it doesn't consider the optimal placement of new tickets. We need to consider the zones of all upcoming trips to minimize the number of coupons. A more effective strategy would be to use dynamic programming, where we keep track of the minimum number of coupons needed for each possible end zone and time.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_dc039c_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_9e3ebd9640",
        "created_at": 1794533080.9364939
      },
      "rev_n_2_ffff65_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_ffff65_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_ffff65",
        "thought_text": "The error in the previous solution was that it didn't consider the case where Johan could buy a new ticket at any point, even if he already has a valid ticket. This approach missed opportunities to optimize the coupon usage. The correct strategy should be to always buy a new ticket when Johan starts a trip, regardless of whether he has a valid ticket or not. This ensures that Johan always has the minimum number of coupons needed for each trip.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_ffff65_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_85803afbfd",
        "created_at": 1794533117.975659
      },
      "rev_n_3_72f86a_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_72f86a_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_72f86a",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of buying a new ticket whenever Johan moves to a new zone without a valid ticket is incorrect. Johan should only buy a new ticket if the current zone is different from the previous one and there's no valid ticket covering the entire trip. This strategy fails for the given example where Johan should have bought a ticket for the first trip to cover both zones 0 and 1.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_72f86a_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_2768f9dfb8",
